// dsv4-token-run.bml -- the measurement door of the Form-native DeepSeek-V4 token path: the real prefill and the greedy decode loop, ONE row a token read from the landed op ledger, the machine beside the clock.
//
//   echo '{"dry":1}' | ./fkwu observe/dsv4-token-run.bml     the plan: the run, the command structure, the dispatches a token (the ledger's formula over the real header) and the ceilings a row is held to, the bytes a token
//                                                              reads and what they cost at a stated bandwidth, the hold rules, the layer prices, the organs of ours resident. Reads the file's header window and the process
//                                                              list; opens nothing, maps nothing, takes no lease, writes no row. Empty stdin and {} do the same: THE DEFAULT IS THE PLAN.
//   echo '{"go":1}' | ./fkwu observe/dsv4-token-run.bml      THE RUN. Not run by the session that wrote it: it asks for the lead's go. Under the governor (the stage asks with their back-off, and the lease, as the
//                                                              validation window makes them) it opens the real file, prefills the 14 pinned prompt ids and runs the decode loop through dsv4-token-handle.fk, and prints one ledger row
//                                                              a token (dll-line: dispatches, barriers, cbs, syncs, readbacks, allocs, bytes, gpu_us, wall_ms, miss; then wired growth, pageins, the device's own bytes), then the
//                                                              summary (the cold first token, the warm decode's ms and tokens a second, the totals). The wired memory is read after EVERY LAYER of the first tokens, without a sync, and
//                                                              the encoding stops BEFORE the machine is at risk (host-memory-low, wired above pct percent of memory, available under the reserve, 20 minutes): the receipt keeps the curve.
//
// stdin, one JSON line, all optional: go, dry, file (the IQ2XXS build by default), cap (64), steps (decode tokens, 24), watch (tokens read after every layer, 3), pct (the wired stop, 60), bw_gbs (546, the stated
// bandwidth the plan prices bytes at), logits_prompt_ids, receipt (receipts/dsv4-token-runs.jsonl).
//
// Before it starts the door checks, and refuses on any: no other model door resident (the process rows flp-gpu-holders reads, a ds4 process, another copy of the validation window), no lease another process holds,
// the machine not low, the file a deepseek4 GGUF with a consistent layout and no tensor the driver cannot run. Every rule, row and the run itself are definitions of form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-token-run.bml, read there and held
// by its bands. Exit: 0 for a completed run with every handle released, 1 otherwise (a hold is not a completion).
// Check the machine first: ./fkwu observe/memory-governor-run.bml </dev/null must show room; run nothing else against the GPU while the door is open.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-token-run.bml
section [form.bml] {
 dtr-main();
}
